From 23e8513366b6dda97897818eef0e4cad3ed8177f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ben Siraphob <bensiraphob@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 19 Apr 2026 12:47:54 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] ldb: tests: fix test_ldb_comparison_fold on platforms with
 32-bit uintptr_t

The STR_VAL() macro used discard_const() to drop const from string
literal initializers, which expands to ((void *)((uintptr_t)(ptr))).
On platforms (or waf configure misdetections) where
sizeof(uintptr_t) < sizeof(void *), this truncates the pointer and
- more importantly - clang (and other strict C compilers) rejects the
pointer->integer->pointer roundtrip as a non-constant expression in a
static initializer, so the whole ranked_value[] array fails to compile
with "initializer element is not a compile-time constant".

Since the STR_VAL inputs are always string literals, a direct
(uint8_t *) cast (matching the type of struct ldb_val.data) is both a
valid constant expression and sufficient to strip const, so drop the
discard_const indirection here.

Observed on aarch64-darwin with samba 4.22.x under nixpkgs, where
waf's uintptr_t probe was misdetecting the type as 'unsigned int'.

Signed-off-by: Ben Siraphob <bensiraphob@gmail.com>
---
 lib/ldb/tests/test_ldb_comparison_fold.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/lib/ldb/tests/test_ldb_comparison_fold.c b/lib/ldb/tests/test_ldb_comparison_fold.c
index 6c5a75e..e61ce73 100644
--- a/lib/ldb/tests/test_ldb_comparison_fold.c
+++ b/lib/ldb/tests/test_ldb_comparison_fold.c
@@ -53,7 +53,7 @@ struct ranked_value {
 	int rank;
 };
 
-#define STR_VAL(s, r) { { discard_const(s), sizeof(s) - 1 }, r}
+#define STR_VAL(s, r) { { (uint8_t *)(s), sizeof(s) - 1 }, r}
 
 static const struct ranked_value values_common[] = {
 	STR_VAL("", 0),
-- 
2.53.0

